<title>HONDURAS: Honduran protest traps, then frees, state workers.</title>
<headline>Honduran protest traps, then frees, state workers.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honduran Economy Minister Fernando Garcia and more than 100 other government workers were freed Monday after being trapped inside the Economy Ministry in a protest against the rising cost of living.</p>
<p>Protesters blocked the exits to the Economy Ministry building for about five hours, but relented when Garcia agreed to meet with protest leaders on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
